{"shortDescription":"Spot basis bids for hard red winter wheat held steady in the southern US Plains on Thursday, spot checks showed, while producers focused on harvesting autumn crops and planting the 2027 winter wheat crop.Basis values are quoted against futures in cts/bu:NOTES: U = K.C. September contract; UNQ = Unq…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot basis bids for hard red winter wheat held steady in the southern US Plains on Thursday, spot checks showed, while producers focused on harvesting autumn crops and planting the 2027 winter wheat crop."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Warm and dry weather this week has helped accelerate winter wheat planting after delays tied to excessive dryness in mid-September and then heavy rains into early October."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The showers recharged soil moisture and reduced drought in top winter wheat producer Kansas as well as Nebraska and Colorado. In Kansas, severe drought covered 10% of the state as of October 6, down from 23% a week earlier, the weekly US Drought Monitor report showed."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Drought remained a concern in Oklahoma despite some weekly improvement. Nearly 43% of the state remained under extreme drought, according to the Drought Monitor, down from 55% the prior week."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["K.C. December hard red winter wheat (KWZ26) futures settled down 2-1/4 cents on Thursday at $7.36-1/4 per bushel as brokers adjusted positions ahead of the USDA's monthly supply/demand reports due Friday."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Analysts surveyed by Reuters on average expected the government on Friday to raise its forecast of US 2026/27 wheat ending stocks to 721 million bushels from 717 million last month."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Protein premiums were mixed. Premi